summary:
Today z0int reaches Hermes in two ways, and neither has measured value on real Hermes traffic yet.

(1) LIVE path: harness-adapters/hermes-z0intelligence. It registers one pre_llm_call hook, starts a `python -m z0int.automatic` subprocess on every turn (about 60 ms median even when disabled) and posts to the local service on 127.0.0.1:11501. It only acts when ~/.z0int/config/automatic.json sets hermes.enabled=true AND the user message exactly matches the regex `Claim:...\nEvidence:...`. Only then does it call paid TypeSafe jev-1.13.0 (evidence_sufficiency: 46/48 and 36/36 on its corpora). It injects about 2.9 KB (about 730 tokens) of receipt JSON into the user message and never skips a frontier call. Real traffic almost never matches the regex. prove-hermes.py passed 9/9 checks, but it imports the adapter directly and never runs Hermes.

(2) SHADOW path, fork-only: kvnloo/hermes-agent PRs #385, #386 and #387 (lab/z0int/*), tracked by #319, #322 and #323. Together they add a metadata-only observer plugin, the first outcome-grounded question `api.attempt_will_fail`, and a Brier/calibration gate hard-coded to promotion_ready=false. CI skipped the Python tests, and no receipt cohort has been collected.

The adapters/hermes_z0int identity helper is used only by its own unit test. Its trace_id is the session_id, while automatic.py and #385 use sha256(session\0turn), so their records cannot be joined.

The z0int evidence base is mostly negative or narrow, and that is valuable. Delegation was PARENT_ONLY: tiny tasks added +1347 uncached parent tokens, and workflow overhead was 30.8 s. Julia-1 and Laya lost to a 5-line keyword rule on real trace data (0.104 and 0.195 vs 0.740, sealed n=77). That study also found the Hermes episode corpus from state.db is degenerate: 76,970 rows but only 1,644 distinct prompts. Jev's hard-coded accuracy of 95.1% is the only strong typed-decision result. Routine compiler and cascade results are synthetic only. The OMP-side wins (a NanoJev cascade cut 61% of Hammer-3B calls at n=28; Hammer-3B behind the compiler matches a 10x slower ladder) have no native Hermes seam, because Hermes' frontier model picks its own tools.

Upstream policy decides placement. A z0int integration is a third-party product, so it must be a standalone plugin repo plus a SHA-pinned plugin-catalog YAML (typesafe-skill-router #112612 was merged that way; in-tree Jev PRs #114376 and #113847 were closed). The generic DecisionProvider runtime (NousResearch#113008, #113020, P3) needs at least 2 independent consumers first. Core changes are realistic only as small hook-payload additions that a real consumer uses.

The strongest next moves need no frontier spend and are mostly offline:
- a per-turn Hermes decision dataset extractor from state.db;
- unifying the identity contract;
- the observer on/off equivalence test plus a receipt cohort;
- using Hermes' own verification_evidence.db and approval/skill hooks as independent outcome labels;
- a BM25 context.filter on web_extract via transform_tool_result;
- a cron "routine miner" that targets Hermes' existing monitor_script/no_agent gating. A third-party fleet reports about 79% of turns are cron/kanban boilerplate.

features.description:
Promote fork PR #385 (lab/z0_hermes_observer). It registers 11 hooks; every callback returns None and fails open. It writes z0int.hermes_observer_event.v1 JSONL to plugin_data_dir with stable per-turn trace_id=sha256(session\0turn), and captures no content by default (raw request/response only with Z0INT_HERMES_CAPTURE_SANITIZED_CONTENT=1).

It should then gain:
- the missing outcome hooks: on_skill_lifecycle, pre/post_approval_request, subagent_start, on_session_finalize, agent_loop_stopped, kanban worker exits;
- the missing scalars: first_chunk_at (TTFB), context_length, middleware_trace length;
- the hermes-jev-skills observer disciplines: a stable-hash sample rate, max-inflight drop with a recorded skip reason, and queue_delay_ms kept separate from backend latency.

Ship it as a standalone plugin repo. Suggested staging branch: promo/z0-observer-v1.

features.hermes_integration_point:
Plugin only, no core edits:
- ctx.register_hook for on_session_start, pre_llm_call (returns None), pre/post_api_request, api_request_error, pre/post_auxiliary_call, pre/post_tool_call, subagent_stop, on_session_end;
- storage via plugins/plugin_storage.plugin_data_dir;
- payload fields verified against agent/turn_api_request.py:64, agent/turn_response_intake.py:69 and agent/api_request_hooks.py:177.

features.description:
This applies the z0int Routine Compiler thesis (repeated cognition moves to the cheapest representation that still passes its verifier) to Hermes' biggest repeated-cognition source. Hermes cron already supports two deterministic modes: monitor_script/monitor_url, which runs first each tick and suppresses the agent run when output is unchanged, and no_agent script jobs.

The miner works offline:
- scan cron and kanban session history for agent runs whose delivered output was unchanged or a no-op given their inputs;
- propose monitor_script gating or no_agent conversion with z0int credit gates (train/dev/sealed/future cohorts, independent-run support floors, Wilson interval, fail-open, demote on a missed change);
- emit a `hermes cron edit` suggestion through a skill.

No learned model runs in the hot path. The agent run is simply skipped when deterministic monitors prove nothing changed.

harness-adapters/hermes-z0intelligence/__init__.py (29 lines) is the only z0int path that changes Hermes behavior. Problems:
- every turn spawns `python -m z0int.automatic event` even when disabled, about 60 ms median import cost in a local microbenchmark;
- when enabled it adds a second spawn ('consume') plus two HTTP calls and a linear receipt scan;
- it locates z0int via Path(__file__).parents[2]/'src', so it only works inside the z0int checkout and cannot be a standalone or catalog plugin;
- it injects the full dispatch JSON as context, about 2,914 chars (about 730 tokens), where a ~100-char verdict would do;
- it triggers only on an exact 'Claim:/Evidence:' regex, so organic coverage is near zero (structural; unmeasured);
- it never records an outcome (no close_observation or join_outcome);
- no in-repo test covers it. prove-hermes.py drives the adapter module directly, not a Hermes process.

Hardening means:
- an in-process client with the z0int path from plugin config;
- an early disabled short-circuit with no spawn;
- a compact verdict injection;
- on_session_end outcome joins;
- a real-Hermes E2E with a temp HERMES_HOME.

Otherwise demote it to observer-only until a contract with real Hermes traffic exists.

z0int has 0 skill_routing events (julia-claims INSUFFICIENT_DATA). Hermes emits on_skill_lifecycle (successful skill lifecycle facts) and supports per-turn user-message hints through pre_llm_call. That is the shape of the TypeSafe skill-router precedent.

Plan:
- capture skill loads, plus whether a suggested skill was loaded, per turn through the observer;
- build a grouped dataset;
- compare deterministic rules (name/keyword), Laya, OpenJev-4B direct logits and, as an optional paid reference, Jev or typesafe-skill-router, on wrong-skill and needless-load rates and latency.

This is the most likely second independent consumer that would make NousResearch#113008's decision-provider bar reachable.

Upstream explicitly will not build the generic host runtime until there are at least two independent bounded-decision consumers with duplicated probability, abstention, privacy and replay semantics. Until then, plugin-local logic and ctx.llm.complete_structured remain the surfaces.

z0int's contribution is evidence, not code. Candidate consumers that share the same semantics: skill routing, the verification gate (pre_verify), API retry classification, smart-approval classification and group-chat response gating (#32692). Measured z0int facts to carry forward:
- confidence is often unusable as a gate (Julia AUROC about 0.47; coverage at a 10% error budget 1.79% / 0.00%);
- placement and precision change verdicts (bf16 vs fp32 flips);
- state rendering is a correctness variable (151/2000 lost to serialization);
- 'execution complete' must stay distinct from verified success.

Extend evaluate_shadow.py (#387) to:
- run grouped bootstrap CIs by session, work item and task family;
- report risk/coverage curves and false-confidence rate (z0int#55);
- compare paired against deterministic rules and logistic controls on the same frozen cohort;
- track self-agreement and threshold-flip rate for repeated readings (z0int#14);
- emit z0eval.hermes_stack_experiment.v0 receipts (schema on lab/evals/hermes-stack-receipts-v0@22b0c745d5, arms H0/Z/R/S/ZR/ZS/RS/ZRS) for z0evals freezing.

The gate keeps promotion_ready=false until a sealed cohort is scored through an API the evolver cannot read (the ABAB_ITERATION_REPORT wave 3 discipline).
